title: No container archive endpoints - docker cp has no equivalent
updated: 2026-08-27T06:34:48Z
---

Three endpoints, none exposed:

  GET  /containers/{id}/archive?path=  - read a path out as a tar stream
  PUT  /containers/{id}/archive?path=  - write a tar stream into a path
  HEAD /containers/{id}/archive?path=  - stat it, no body

Together they are what "docker cp" is built on, and they are the only way to
get a file in or out of a container without exec plus shell quoting.

Notes for whoever takes it:
- GET returns a raw tar stream, not JSON. _request decodes bodies; this one
  must come back as bytes. Same requirement as images->get in the sibling
  ticket, so solve the raw-body case once.
- HEAD answers with an X-Docker-Container-Path-Stat header holding
  base64-encoded JSON, and no body at all. A HEAD path through _request may
  not exist yet.
- PUT takes the tarball as the request body with a noOverwriteDirNonDir and
  a copyUIDGID query parameter.

